  "slug": "fresh-tortilla-triangles",
  "name": "Fresh Tortilla Triangles",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "Not only is this relatively inexpensive, but it's also easy to make! And, these chips can be cooled and stored in an airtight container for two days.",
  "cuisine": "Mexican Inspired American Mexican",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Heat oil in a 10-inch skillet to 370 degrees. Drop triangles in hot oil, 8 at a time. Fry, turning chips once or twice, until they stop sizzling and turn golden brown, about 2 minutes. Remove with tongs or a slotted spoon and drain on a wire rack set over a shallow pan. Sprinkle with salt immediately."
    }
  ],
